## Assumptions and limitations
No eligible matched Schwann Nae1-by-Nrf2 design with PMP22 nascent output was established in this bounded search. This is not proof of absence, not evidence that the response must be parallel, and not a new causal claim. Independent perturbation precedents exist in other compartments: retinal MLN4924 x siNrf2 (PMC12596376); skin Nedd8/Nrf2 factorial metadata (GSE326641). Schwann nuclear/necessity-assay precedents exist for other interventions/endpoints (PMC3863807; PMC6497605). These constrain assay feasibility, not cross-context transfer.

GSE326641 batch 2 has one labelled library each for N8_Ctrl, NEDD8_KO, NRF2_KO and NEDD8_NRF2_KO. Independent donors/pools and elapsed post-recombination time are unresolved. K14 skin targeting and 3-prime steady-state RNA cannot identify Schwann Nae1/PMP22 promoter mediation. RDS not downloaded or executed. GSE326639 provides related skin Xenium data, also not a calibrated nascent assay. Adjacent candidate GSE326642 returned HTTP 200 private HTML, not SOFT; no sibling relationship or biological measurements inferred. Original title/genotype inconsistencies remain literal.

The audit preserves the inherited shared-feature count (12,496) and conditional source mapping; it checks only 13 declared genes, not a redefined feature universe. Nae1 inputs are RSEM expected counts, not assumed integer molecules; Figlia counts are source-normalized. The repeated Dev1/2/3 controls do not become independent across contrasts. Four labelled Nae1 libraries per group do not establish litter/pool independence.

