## Open questions
The bounded audit is complete; the biology is unresolved. A new within-donor four-arm Nae1-loss x genetic-Nrf2-loss experiment, with verified early target engagement, independent biological preparations, nuclear NRF2 and calibrated endogenous Pmp22 nascent output, is a feasible next test subject to a kinetics/state-overlap pilot. Assess EGR2 and state prospectively; use selective NRF2 addback and a separate EGR2 rescue. An antioxidant program that disappears while Pmp22 suppression remains supports separation; relief of suppression supports dependence; worsening supports compensation, conditional on specificity and state/viability overlap. Exposed antioxidant genes remain engagement controls, not newly locked validation. Protein-only rescue cannot answer promoter mediation. Lack of a jointly engaged, viable, comparable-state window is a design failure, not a covariate-adjustment opportunity.
